[Event "01 - The Queen's Gambit Decision"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLUjxDD7HNNTgUtmFtlWp2W3Lu9RKRziZv"]
[Date "2025.??.??"]
[Round "1"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 {The c-pawn asks how Black will support d5. Before exchanging, read whether a pawn or piece will recapture.} 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 Be7 6. e3 O-O 7. Bd3 c6 8. Nge2 Nbd7 9. Qc2 Re8 10. O-O {The Exchange QGD gives White the lasting choice between b4-b5 and f3-e4.} *

[Event "02 - Exchange QGD with Bf4"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a4qOTCiVejg&t=1267s"]
[Date "2025.??.??"]
[Round "2"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "QGD - early Be7"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Be7 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bf4 {With Black's bishop already on e7, Bf4 develops outside the chain before e3.} 5... c6 6. e3 Bf5 7. g4 {A practical way to question Black's active bishop; calculate before advancing around your king.} 7... Bg6 8. h4 h5 9. g5 Qb6 10. Qd2 Nd7 11. Nf3 *

[Event "03 - Carlsbad Planning Position"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PtBjKCVo2so&t=397s"]
[Date "2025.??.??"]
[Round "3"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "QGD - Carlsbad"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 Be7 6. e3 O-O 7. Bd3 c6 8. Nge2 Nbd7 9. Qc2 Re8 10. O-O {White should now choose a plan. The queenside route is b4-b5 against c6; the central route is f3-e4. Do not launch either plan before checking Black's immediate tactics and freeing breaks.} *

[Event "04 - Early c5 and the IQP"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bJ-a-RGsmAo&t=300s"]
[Date "2025.??.??"]
[Round "4"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "Tarrasch structure"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 e6 2. c4 d5 3. Nc3 c5 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. g3 {The fianchetto develops without blocking the c1-bishop and puts pressure on d5.} 6... Nf6 7. Bg2 Be7 8. O-O O-O 9. dxc5 Bxc5 {Black's isolated d-pawn can be active, but it is also a permanent target. Blockade first, then simplify the active pieces.} 10. Bg5 Be6 11. Rc1 Be7 12. Nd4 *

[Event "05 - Queen's Gambit Accepted: 3.e4"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iKZfZ03Qhlo&t=727s"]
[Date "2025.??.??"]
[Round "5"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "Queen's Gambit Accepted"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. e4 {Aman's immediate recommendation: use the time Black spent on the wing to occupy the centre.} 3... c5 4. d5 {Keep the space and avoid an automatic liquidation.} 4... e6 5. Nc3 exd5 6. Nxd5 Nf6 7. Bxc4 Nxe4 8. Qe2 {The pin makes the central knight tactically vulnerable.} 8... f5 9. f3 Be6 10. fxe4 Bxd5 11. exd5+ *

[Event "06 - Queen's Gambit Accepted: the a4 Lever"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MrLtRMvMjmg&t=1115s"]
[Date "2025.??.??"]
[Round "6"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "QGA - Black holds c4"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. e4 b5 4. a4 {Attack the base of Black's pawn chain instead of chasing c4 move by move.} 4... c6 5. axb5 cxb5 6. b3 Qc7 7. bxc4 bxc4 8. Nf3 Bg4 9. Nc3 e6 10. Qa4+ Nd7 11. Ne5 {Development and pressure make the extra c-pawn impossible to enjoy.} *

[Event "07 - Slav: Challenge the Bishop"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IJumW5CW5DM&t=1331s"]
[Date "2025.??.??"]
[Round "7"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "Slav"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 c6 2. c4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. e3 Bf5 5. Nf3 e6 6. Nh4 {Black delayed e6 to release this bishop; make it spend more time.} 6... Bg6 7. Qb3 Qb6 8. Nxg6 hxg6 9. Bd3 Nbd7 10. Qc2 {Other recurring tools are h3-g4, Ne5, and pressure on b7/d5 with Qb3.} *

[Event "08 - Nimzo-Indian: Qc2"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IJumW5CW5DM&t=499s"]
[Date "2025.??.??"]
[Round "8"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "Nimzo-Indian"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qc2 {The repertoire move preserves options: e4 is supported and Qxc3 can avoid doubled pawns.} 4... O-O 5. Nf3 d5 6. a3 Bxc3+ 7. Qxc3 c5 8. dxc5 Ne4 9. Qc2 Qa5+ 10. b4 Qc7 11. e3 a5 12. Bb2 {Use the bishop pair, central expansion, and rooks on the open files.} *

[Event "09 - King's Indian: Bd3 and Nge2"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CoRKyhLFc8I&t=937s"]
[Date "2025.??.??"]
[Round "9"]
[White "Aman Hambleton repertoire"]
[Black "King's Indian"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Bd3 O-O 6. Nge2 {This supports the centre while keeping the f-pawn free.} 6... e5 7. d5 Nbd7 8. O-O Ne8 9. h3 f5 10. exf5 gxf5 11. f4 {The closed centre makes a kingside expansion coherent; do not rush it before castling.} *

